		<cell><p>When you submit this script, it must be a single self-contained <pf>.m</pf> file that can be run without any other files in the same directory.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This means you have to include ALL the functions (i.e. "helper functions") that this script needs to run at the bottom of the script. The screenshot below illustrates the structure of such a script. Note that only the first three helper functions are displayed.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Before submitting your final script, I highly recommend placing your script in a separate folder with no other programs. Then run that script. If it runs as intended without any errors, it should be ready to submit.</p></cell>
